From c3b229898aa175a442598f7dbecf0b85cc63e0b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: svend-blip <svend@torplarsen.dk>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:31:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(moe): TierInfer-served expert banks for CPU-executor
 layers

With TIERINFER_SOCK set (a running `tierinfer serve <ftw-dir> --ram-gb N`)
and --moe-cpu-layers naming the CPU-executor layers, those layers' banks
take HostResidency.TIERED: an anonymous buffer TierInfer fills per expert
row on first touch from the FTW shards and evicts under its budget, in
place of the load-time O_DIRECT fill. GPU layers keep the pinned banks and
the slot cache; pin()/lock() refuse a tiered bank (both would fault the
whole bank in). Flat-region banks refuse tiering (rows must be
addressable per layer). The CPU executor logs each tiered layer's ids to
a per-layer pinned buffer inside the step and reports them to TierInfer
before the next step (ROUTED: after the fact, since a graph replay leaves
Python out of the step). Unpatched configurations are unchanged.
